{
  "_comment": "The person picker across the Mac bridge (docs/design-people.md § UX iteration 3). Vitest (frontend/src/utils/personPickerBridge.test.ts) builds each web_to_native `wire` from `input` with the English strings, and resolves each native_to_web `payload` against its `slot` to `effect`. Swift (BristlenoseTests/PersonPickerContractTests.swift) decodes every `wire` exactly as BridgeHandler receives it and builds every `payload` from `native`. Change a shape here first, then both sides. Version 3 (6 Oct 2026, design-people.md §J8): rows carry their own codes, the new row the next free one, and a reply says which row it came from — a listed name, a typed one (`new`) or That's Me (`me`) — so a typed name is never read as a pick. A reply the SPA refuses resolves to `{\"taken\": name}`. Version 4 (6 Oct 2026): the ✕ — native replies `{\"kind\": \"clear\"}`, carrying no name, and the SPA applies it only where the slot holds a moderator or observer (§J8.8). Version 5 (6 Oct 2026): rename in place — native replies `{\"kind\": \"rename\", \"name\": …}` for the current, confirmed row; the SPA refuses a taken name and treats it as a new spelling for that person everywhere (§J8.16). Version 6 (6 Oct 2026): a recode (§J7 R1) — web sends `roles`, the other roles the speaker can move to, each with its own rows, codes and next code (built from `knownByRole`, the people by role); native replies with `role` when the pick was made under another role, and the SPA resolves it as that person, or someone new, in that role. Version 7 (6 Oct 2026): R2 — every role is open on every speaker. `roles` carries `participant` for a moderator or observer (only the speaker themself, numbered after every participant) and `moderator`/`observer` for a participant (the team; a participant has no uuid to offer as themself); `newPromptFor.participant` arrives with its number filled. Replies may carry `role: participant`. Version 8 (6 Oct 2026): the swap (§J7 call 4) — web sends `swap`, the code of the speaker this one would exchange with, in a session of exactly one participant and one moderator; labels carry `swapWith` with `{{code}}` left for native; native replies `{\"kind\": \"swap\"}`, which the SPA applies only where it offered one. Version 9 (6 Oct 2026): the transcript's Session | Paragraph switch (design-people.md §K) — labels carry `scope` (the two words and the group's name); from a paragraph's badge web sends `scope`, whether it opens on Paragraph and this session's speakers (`code`, `slot`, `name`, `role`); native replies `{\"kind\": \"paragraph\", \"slot\": …}` for a paragraph pick, which the SPA applies only to a speaker it offered. Any other reply from a scoped picker was made on Session. Under the Paragraph scope's Moderator, a new-moderator row replies `{\"kind\": \"paragraph\", \"new\": \"moderator\"}`; serve makes the session an unknown moderator and moves the paragraph to them.",
